# Konnect MCP quirks

Add new entries here as they are discovered. Longer reference: `KICAD_KONNECT_GUIDE.md` in the repo root.

1. `add_power_symbol` takes `power_net` (for example `"+5V"` or `"GND"`), not `lib_id`.
   Passing `lib_id` fails with `invalid_argument: power_net missing`.
2. KiCad editor lock: if the schematic is open in KiCad, every schematic write fails
   (`stale_target`, `mutation_outcome_uncertain`, or `conflict` with "KiCad editor lock").
   Ask the user to close the schematic editor before editing, and grep the file to confirm nothing was written before retrying.
   PCB tools use live IPC, so the PCB editor may stay open.
3. Schematic placement snaps to the 1.27 mm grid. Pick on-grid coordinates up front.
4. No DNP-flag tool and no schematic text-delete tool. Convey DNP in the Value text (e.g. "(DNP)"),
   or have the user set the attribute in KiCad. Delete text with `batch_delete` using its uuid.
5. `batch_edit_schematic_components` requires `schematic` and `edits: [{reference, value?, footprint?, fields?}]`.
   Custom fields are only created when `create_missing` is true.
6. `rotate_schematic_component` takes an absolute rotation, not a delta.
7. Power symbol orientation: rotation 0 points down, 90 extends right, 180 points up, 270 extends left.
8. Wire crossings need no junction. Junctions are needed at T-connections and where 3 or more items meet.
9. Wire-only nets get auto names like `Net-(J4-Pin_1)`. To keep stable PCB net names,
   place a net label on one wire per net. Netlist names carry a `/` prefix.
10. `add_schematic_component` supports `mirror` ('x'/'y') and `rotation`.
    `Conn_01x04` at rotation 180 puts pins on the right. `Conn_02x03_Odd_Even` with mirror `y`
    puts odd pins right of the origin and even pins left.
11. `list_schematic_wires` returns wire uuids, which `batch_delete` accepts alongside references.
12. Prefer batch tools (`batch_add_wire`, `batch_add_junction`, `batch_edit_schematic_components`,
    `batch_delete`) over repeated single calls.
13. `render_schematic_png` output is small. Use `check_schematic_overlaps` for overlap checks.
14. Never edit `.kicad_*` files directly. Verify every change with readback, ERC and DRC.
15. No PCB tool to move/resize footprint Reference/Value silk text. `edit_component` is
    value-only; `list_board_footprint_graphics` omits property text. Use KiCad
    Edit → Edit Text & Graphics Properties, Scripting Console (`SetFPRelativePosition`),
    or Computer Use — not Konnect MCP.
16. Always ask the user before starting PCB work. The user opens `*.kicad_pcb` in the
    PCB editor for you; do not try to open or drive pcbnew yourself (Computer Use /
    `launch_kicad_ui` alone is not enough, and this KiCad build’s IPC
    `GetOpenDocuments` is often `AS_UNHANDLED`).
17. Custom `create_symbol` pin angles: tip coordinates are the electrical ends.
    Left-side tips use angle `0` (pin points right into the body), right-side `180`,
    top `270`, bottom `90` — same as KiCad’s own library symbols. Using the opposite
    angles leaves a visible gap between pin and body.
